        for the claimant 1.\n\nThe income should then be treated as the claimant’s income 2.\n\n\nNote:
        In SPC a member of a couple is referred to as a partner and both members are referred to as\n\n\
        partners3. DMG 77117.6 gives guidance that a person subject to immigration control should be treated\n\
        as not being a member of the same household. The income of a partner subject to immigration control\n\
        should not be treated as the claimant's income.\n\n\n                                        \
        \       1 SPC Regs, reg 14; 2 SPC Act 02, s 5; 3 SPC Regs, reg 1(3)"
      locator: DMG 85016
